%% The four names behind one Afs private endpoint - which one carries which conversation, and what happens when only three of them resolve
%% Source: Microsoft Learn - Configure Azure File Sync network endpoints (the private endpoint publishes mysssmanagement, myssssyncp, myssssyncs and mysssmonitoring under privatelink.afs.azure.net, group id Afs, incomingTrafficPolicy AllowAllTraffic or AllowVirtualNetworksOnly, no service endpoint option); codex/blueprint-azure-file-sync-private-path.md step 3; codex/runbook-file-sync-broken-after-network-lockdown.md class 3
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant SRV as Registered server on contoso.local
  participant IB as Infoblox grid
  participant RES as Private Resolver inbound endpoint
  participant ZONE as Zone privatelink.afs.azure.net
  participant PE as Private endpoint pe-sss-afs, four IP configurations
  participant SSS as Storage Sync Service
  participant SA as Storage account file endpoint

  Note over SRV,SSS: One endpoint, four host names. The pattern is sssname plus management, syncp, syncs and monitoring, each prefixed to region dot afs.azure.net

  SRV->>IB: sssname-management.region.afs.azure.net ?
  IB->>RES: forwarded because the public answer is a CNAME into privatelink.afs.azure.net
  RES->>ZONE: lookup A
  ZONE-->>SRV: 10.51.x.11
  SRV->>PE: HTTPS 443 to the management name
  PE->>SSS: registration and management calls, server registration record and configuration

  SRV->>PE: HTTPS 443 to the monitoring name 10.51.x.14
  PE->>SSS: agent telemetry and health, the feed behind the StorageSyncServerHeartbeat metric

  loop every 30 seconds
    SRV->>PE: HTTPS 443 GetNextJob on the primary sync name syncp 10.51.x.12
    PE->>SSS: job poll
    SSS-->>SRV: status 0, written to Telemetry event 9301
  end

  SRV->>PE: HTTPS 443 sync session on syncp, with syncs 10.51.x.13 as the secondary sync channel
  PE->>SSS: metadata, change batches and cloud endpoint coordination
  SSS-->>SRV: session result, written to Telemetry event 9102 with HResult 0

  Note over SRV,SA: File bytes never travel on any afs name. Upload, download and recall go to the storage account file endpoint on its own private endpoint and its own zone
  SRV->>SA: HTTPS 443 FileREST through pe-account-file

  alt one of the four names is missing from the zone or from the forwarder
    SRV->>IB: sssname-syncs.region.afs.azure.net ?
    IB-->>SRV: public IP or NXDOMAIN
    SRV->>SRV: Debug-StorageSyncServer -TestNetworkConnectivity fails on that one name only
    Note over SRV,SSS: While incomingTrafficPolicy is still AllowAllTraffic the agent falls back to the public path and nothing looks broken. This is the trap
    SRV->>SSS: same call over the public endpoint
  else the policy was already set to AllowVirtualNetworksOnly
    SRV->>SSS: call refused, there is no public path left
    SSS-->>SRV: no answer, 9301 stops returning status 0
    Note over SRV,SSS: Every registered server on this Storage Sync Service goes to Appears Offline, not just this one. Assessor AFS-11 and NET-05
    SRV->>SSS: rollback Set-AzStorageSyncService -IncomingTrafficPolicy AllowAllTraffic restores sync in minutes
  end

  Note over SRV,ZONE: The gate before the policy change is all four names returning 10.x on EVERY registered server. Three out of four is a failed gate, and a hosts file entry is a testing workaround, never the production answer
